    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Gotcha. One thing that worries me is that sometimes things just seem to fail for no reason, even when you've followed the specs and the wood looks fine. Like, you see a joint start to pull apart or a beam suddenly crack after a few seasons. Is there anything else that could cause these random points of failure or \"hidden\" weaknesses that I should look out for during the build?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "One common culprit for seemingly random failures is moisture entrapment, which can lead to rot or fastener corrosion within joints, even if the wood initially appears sound. Inadequate drainage around posts can also introduce constant moisture, accelerating decay at critical load-bearing points. Always ensure all connections are perfectly snug and that any wood touching concrete or ground is adequately protected against moisture contact.",
      "source": "target",
